  "description": "Calibration approaches the body as a field of forces held in a programmed balance. \nThe structure translates invisible force into contour, rhythm and a provisional anatomy.\n\nEchoing the logic of the hydrostatic skeleton, the form emerges through the dependency of softness and constraint. Neither fixed nor freely expanded, it remains suspended between compression and release.\n\n“In short, the form of an object is a ‘diagram of forces.’”\n D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form, 1917",
